  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "I9d/oVDHqQk780YUQU8tFmdviGA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:25.084Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The session recorded a \"long tail of community banks and insurers\", \"potentially well connected\", with an established consultancy market \u2014 qualified immediately by \"but it may be dominated by the big players only\". Both PMF and companion-software candidates are marked unresolved.\n\nThe countervailing observation is the interesting one: \"software / app support is becoming increasingly a large part of the value proposition of banks/insurers\". If true, the addressable spend grows without the institutions consolidating, which is exactly the condition that sustains a long tail worth selling into.\n\nThe unresolved question is whether the consultancy channel into that tail exists or whether it terminates at a handful of large firms \u2014 which would break the channel strategy in this sector specifically.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:25.084214Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:25.084218Z"
    }
  },
